&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;“I just finished &lt;/em&gt;Prisoners of Geography&lt;em&gt; by Tim Marshall. I was struck by how much the physical landscape still shapes global politics—technology changes quickly, but mountains, rivers, and coastlines continue to influence the decisions nations can make.”&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
